# Protected paths — the mechanical half of AGENTS.md → Don't-touch list.
#
# One glob per line, relative to the project root; `#` starts a comment.
# `*` crosses `/`; a line naming a directory protects everything beneath it.
# .agentic/hooks/protect-paths.sh refuses an agent edit or write to a
# matching path in every client and tells the agent to ask. This file is
# project-owned: the human edits it; an agent proposes a change and waits.
# Entries that name part of a file (a TOML table) stay prose in AGENTS.md.
#
# Examples — uncomment or add your own:
# src/<package>/migrations/
# sources/
# out/
